@* Not on the booking pages: there the button linked to the page the visitor was already on, and on
   a phone it sat on top of the form's fields (PROJECT_STATE Section 3cb).

   Not on the sign-in pages either (login, forgot password, reset password). They are the admin's,
   so "Book Now" there is addressed to nobody, and on a phone it sat on top of the password box
   (PROJECT_STATE Section 3cc). *@
@{
    var onBookingPages = string.Equals(this.ViewContext.RouteData.Values["controller"] as string, "Booking", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
    var onSignInPages = string.Equals(this.ViewContext.RouteData.Values["area"] as string, "Identity", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
}
@if (!onBookingPages && !onSignInPages)
{
    <div class="mobile-cta-bar">
        <a asp-controller="Booking" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-success btn-mobile-cta">
            Book Now
        </a>
    </div>
}
